    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d995">

                <pb facs="0915" n="905" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg905"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1163 M 56/358</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 6011</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-01-12">January 12,
                        1942</date>.<lb/>[Received August 26.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Embassy’s telegram
                    to the Department No. 1728 of November 1, 3 p.m. (1941),<anchor n="84"
                        xml:id="d995-f1"/> stating that representations had been made with respect
                    to damage inflicted by Japanese armed forces on the property of the American
                    Methodist Mission at various places in Fukien Province, China, I have the honor
                    to enclose, for the record, a translation of a communication from the Japanese
                    Foreign Office dated December 4, 1941,<anchor n="84" xml:id="d995-f2"/>
                    requesting sketch maps showing the exact locations of the damaged properties.
                    War broke out between the United States and Japan before the Embassy could take
                    action in the matter.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph C. Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
